WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.801
-That's what I'm talking about.
Paul Shaffer, right there.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.367
The World's Most Dangerous Band.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.601
-What a trip.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:10.300
This is surreal to be here
after all this time.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.334
-I'm so excited that you're here
and thankful that you're here.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.234
But this is --
When was the first time?

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.534
This has been, what?

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:19.100
-Well, you know,
this is such a coincidence

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.267
that we're here tonight,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.367
because 41 years ago
this very week

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.000
was when David Letterman

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.267
came on the air right here,
right across the hall

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.634
here at NBC --
-Is that right?

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.968
-...with "The Late Show With
David Letterman."

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.167
-Oh, my gosh.
-So, this is, like,

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:34.667
our 41st anniversary
that we're celebrating.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.200
And thanks to you,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.667
I have reunited the entire band
from "The Letterman Show."

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:40.968
We're all here.
-Yes!

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:44.000
That's what I'm talking about.
-All the favorites.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.734
-Boys and girl, and we're just
having the time of our lives,

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:48.801
thanks to you.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:52.534
-When David Letterman
first started,

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.100
he started
as a morning show, right?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.267
-That's right, yes.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.100
-And he asked you
to be the musical director?

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.634
-I got the call from him
to do "The Morning Show."

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.434
It was right after
"Saturday Night."

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.100
I had done
the first five seasons

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.634
of "Saturday Night Live"...
-That's right.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.934
-...as a pianist and a little
bit of performing and writing.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.467
And then I got a call.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.868
David Letterman
is going on the air

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.767
at 10:00 in the morning, live.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.267
And I -- I turned it down.
I turned him down.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:15.534
-You turned it down? Why?
-I did.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.167
-Why?
-Couldn't get up that early.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.667
[ Laughter ]
But No --

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.100
-Why, yeah, of course.
-It just didn't seem --

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.000
I don't know.
You know, but luckily for me,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.167
when that show didn't happen,
they gave him another shot.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.567
They gave him "The Late Show,"
the 12:30 spot.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.767
-Yeah.
-And they called me again.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.434
And this time, I had the sense
enough to say yes.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.868
And you know,
here we are, 33 years later

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.567
between the two networks.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:40.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:44.567
-You know what --
I thought about you,

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:45.834
and I was so happy.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.434
When I used to do Letterman --

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.067
First of all, I was a big fan.
I watched his show.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.200
I watched "Late Night"
all the time.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.367
And I love Dave Letterman.
He's a genius, so funny.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.467
But I remember
when I did the show,

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.567
I would be nervous to meet you.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.100
-Ah.
-Because, yeah.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.634
I mean, I'm such a fan.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.167
And I was, like,
so nervous to be around you

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.434
and meet you guys and watch you.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.267
But you not only
changed the game

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:08.067
and raised the bar of what
a band can do on the show.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.367
Obviously, Doc Severinsen.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:12.367
But then, you showed us how to
take it to a next level.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:16.634
And then I think you changed
the face of comedy as well,

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:17.734
if I may say,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.334
because you would laugh
at a joke --

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.901
You told me backstage,
by the way,

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.734
for the first two episodes,
they didn't turn your mic on.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.400
-Well, that's another story.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.634
But, when they turned your mic
on and Dave told a joke,

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.834
and sometimes the audience
wouldn't really laugh.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.934
But you would go, "Ah."

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.934
And that's when you knew
it was funny.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.968
And comedy nerds
around at home are going,

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.968
"He's right.
That was a funny joke."

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.400
And the audience
just didn't get it yet.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.400
And you just went, "Ah."

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.400
-I didn't know
I had that much responsibility,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.767
but I'm thrilled
to hear it though.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.367
-Now, I think because of you,
comedians everywhere,

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.334
comedians I know,
they all laugh like you.

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.601
-Oh, is that right?
-Every comedian --

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.267
Tina Fey laughs like you.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:01.067
You see a funny joke,
you go, "Ah."

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.100
That's you.
-Ah.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.167
-They're doing you.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.367
-That's Paul Shaffer
right there,

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:05.400
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.300
I'm honored. Honored.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.667
-Jimmy, I am humbled.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.767
-The honor.
Beyond honored that you're here.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.133
-Well, you know,
remember all of us

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.567
looked to Johnny Carson
as our model.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.868
And he used to have
Doc Severinsen at band leader

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.901
and Ed on the panel to talk to.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.567
And I used to say, "I'm
a combination of Doc and Ed."

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.234
In other words, I'm dead.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.434
Basically, I'm dead.
-That's exactly right, yeah.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.334
-But I'm alive tonight.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.200
-Come on.
I'm happy you're here, bud.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.634
♪♪

